      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A known hypertensive presented to the hospital with sudden onset of chest pain and shock. ECG, cardiac enzymes, aortogram and echocardiogram were normal. Hemodynamic monitoring and radionucleotide angiogram demonstrated a severely dyskinetic right ventricle. Autopsy revealed proximal aortic dissection with extramural compression of right coronary artery, resulting in right ventricular dysfunction."},
